WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.300
In this lesson we work with number columns in Power Query, using the Financial Sample table.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:16.100
When a number column is selected, the Transform tab offers Statistics, Standard, Scientific, Trigonometry, and Rounding.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.070
Statistics returns one summary value for the whole column, such as the sum, the

4
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.840
minimum, the maximum, the median, the average, or the standard deviation.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.760
Before we use these tools, it helps to scroll through the data and understand each column:

6
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.140
segment, country, product, discount band, and units sold.

7
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.103
Here I chose Standard Deviation on Units Sold.

8
00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:11.370
The result is a single number, about eight hundred sixty seven.

9
00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.801
Power Query replaced the whole table with this value, so we remove that step

10
00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.740
to get the table back.

11
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.656
Next, the Standard menu.

12
00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:37.038
Add, Multiply, Subtract, Divide, and Percent Of change every value in the column.

13
00:01:37.038 --> 00:01:42.420
For example, Add asks for a number and adds it to each row.

14
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.911
On the Transform tab, these tools change the existing column.

15
00:02:01.911 --> 00:02:07.387
On the Add Column tab, the same tools create a new column and keep

16
00:02:07.387 --> 00:02:12.080
the original, which is safer when you still need the raw values.

17
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.791
Finally, Rounding.

18
00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:36.329
Round Up moves each value to the next whole number, Round Down to the

19
00:02:36.329 --> 00:02:40.284
previous one, and Round lets you choose the decimal places.

20
00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:44.240
Each change appears as a new step under Applied Steps.

